From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 05:35:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] updater: keep the update screen open with progress and an
 Install button
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Tapping "Download" on the new-version screen used to pop the screen at once
and continue in the background: a progress notification, then a silent
PackageInstaller session (API 31+) with a "tap to install" notification as
fallback. Under HarmonyOS 卓易通 neither the notifications nor the installer
session show up, so after tapping Download nothing visible happens and the
user never gets to install the update.

Port Mihon's flow instead. The screen now has a Voyager StateScreenModel
that observes the AppUpdateDownloadJob work info: the button turns into
"Downloading… (xx%)" while the APK downloads, "Install" when it is ready
(the file is handed to the system installer with ACTION_VIEW, which does
work in 卓易通) and "Retry" if the download failed. Leaving the screen
while downloading cancels the download, like Mihon.

AppUpdateDownloadJob publishes progress and the URL through setProgress /
the output data, exposes TAG, PROGRESS and updateApk(), and takes an
`interactive` flag: downloads started from the screen skip the
PackageInstaller session and the install notification, because the screen
handles installing. Notification- and scheduled-run downloads keep the old
behaviour.
